@extremeencounter7458 I'm sorry you're just figuring this out, but the US is going down as a nation. They still have the bigger military (for now), but they obviously don't know how to use it. Having resources is important, but having no strategic mind and no diplomatic skill will make them waste those resources, as we are seing with Iran. Add to that the problems they are going to face inside the US with the economy going down the drain and half the politicians having been shown to be completely corrupt and without anything ressembling a spine, and it's easy to see that the whole place has become a circus. They have become fundamentally unserious as a nation.

I don't like where China is going with all the surveillance and expansionist tendencies, but at least they have some plan for the future other than "making as much money as possible for the leader and his family". That will allow them to easily replace the US as the world's biggest power.

Obviously, something could happen in China that would make them change course, but as it's going right now, the future is pretty clear on that front.

