snippet.textDisplay:
@Kay_R ‘BuILDinG RobOTs’ gives you NO IDEA about algorithmic progress and the state of world models today. Hardware is not software; the actual engineers dealing with hardware here aren’t remotely the ones training the models virtually and there’s no way you cover both specialties enough to definitively know. I doubt you’re an engineer in the first place, nevertheless actually have first principles knowledge about massively parallel processing, machine learning in general at the edge, the limitations of the physical processing power as an edge node, limitations of world models today, etc. I also somewhat doubt you’ve done anything but piecemeal a robot together; designing your own unified control algorithms, sensor suites and feedback loops, and an overarching unified systems architecture is in a completely different wheelhouse to “building robots.” I built my first robot at like 10 years old; as an engineer, building robots doesn’t mean shit. Expand on that or it doesn’t mean a thing, don’t lie either bc there are plenty of engineers in the comments to call you out. 

People are right to suspect tele-operation because most humanoid demos are fudged in some way today; even if not via tele-operation, this has happened constantly in Silicon Valley for 50+ years. This includes Tesla’s Optimus Demos, who absolutely have the best ML team in the world. Figure is not better at world models and local/edge integration than Tesla lmfao. If you think they can be trusted to do this 1000% honestly, you have a lot of Silicon Valley history to catch up on. 

I watched this live; I don’t really recall them actually proving it was 100% autonomous. It seems to me like they hid the lower body of the bot to hide the fact it’s tethered. It did some suspect movements, on livestream that you clearly haven’t seen. Processing 100% locally at the edge is hard given today’s silicon (energy and processing power limitations, model limitations and inefficiency, etc). Even given the sus movement, the robot was missing packages and definitely doing an imperfect job. It’s not even remotely this close of a competition in reality; the variables were tightly controlled to generate hype and you should know this if you have even a shred of knowledge about how engineering something like this works.

